# Dispatch One

A modern, mobile-first emergency dispatch game (Leitstellenspiel-style) built in TypeScript.

## Tech stack

- **Frontend**: Next.js (App Router) on Cloudflare Pages, MapLibre + Protomaps, Tailwind, Zustand, TanStack Query, Socket.IO client, next-intl + Tolgee
- **Backend**: NestJS on Fly.io (REST `/api/v1` + Socket.IO gateway)
- **Worker**: NestJS standalone on Fly.io (spawn engine, salary tick, schedulers)
- **Data**: Neon Postgres + PostGIS, Prisma, Upstash Redis, OSRM (self-hosted)
- **Secrets**: Infisical (envs: `development` / `staging` / `production`)
- **Repo**: pnpm + Turborepo monorepo

## Repository state

This repo currently contains **only docs**. Application code is built phase-by-phase from `docs/dispatch-one-development-roadmap.md` (the plan file). When unsure what phase we're in, read the roadmap.

## Spec doc precedence (when docs conflict)

1. `docs/dispatch-one-decisions.md` — product behaviour
2. `docs/dispatch-one-mvp-implementation-spec.md` — implementation contract
3. `docs/dispatch-one-engineering-decisions.md` — engine, time, spawn, routing
4. `docs/dispatch-one-architecture.md` — infra, security, Infisical, CI/CD
5. `docs/dispatch-one-design-system.md` — UI / UX
6. `docs/dispatch-one-api-design.md` — WebSocket events
7. `docs/dispatch-one-schema.md` — Prisma schema
8. `docs/dispatch-one-testing.md` — test strategy
9. Content sources: `dispatch-one-incidents.md`, `vehicles-*.md`, `dispatch-one-skill-tree.md`
10. `docs/claude_design/V1/` — visual reference only, never feature spec

## Hard rules

- If a behaviour is not defined in a spec doc, **ask before guessing**.
- Never invent fields, endpoints, events, or IDs that are not in `impl-spec`, `api-design`, or `schema`.
- Vehicle / skill / incident IDs are canonical `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` ASCII (`HLF_20`, not `HLF 20`).
- All player-facing strings are i18n keys — no hardcoded English.
- Single repo, no submodules.
